{
 "id": "SHW-25",
 "name": "patient-monitor",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "ICU patient monitor: sweeping ECG, pleth and respiration traces with alarm limits",
 "summary": "A bedside monitor drawn in one canvas: ECG lead II, SpO2 pleth and respiration traces sweep left to right with the erase gap of a real monitor, rebuilt every frame from three small float arrays and the clock; heart rate, SpO2, respiration rate and blood pressure come from host variables, and the HR (or SpO2) tile and a top banner flash red when a value leaves its alarm limits. Landscape on a tablet, numerics under the traces on a phone.",
 "prompt": "Build an ICU-style patient monitor: a scrolling ECG trace drawn from a waveform array looping with the clock, with the sweep-and-erase gap of a real monitor, an SpO2 pleth wave, heart rate and SpO2 numbers from host variables, and a flashing red alarm when the heart rate is out of range. Dark, crisp, legible, on a tablet and on a phone.",
 "level": 5,
 "family": "SHW",
 "capabilities": {
